WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.892
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:16.162 --> 00:18.331
SEOUL

3
00:27.799 --> 00:29.425
-Just trust me, ladies. -Let's go here.

4
00:29.509 --> 00:31.386
Come on, ladies.

5
00:32.470 --> 00:33.596
She's a kid.

6
00:34.264 --> 00:36.808
-She's cute. -Come on, she's a kid.

7
00:47.277 --> 00:48.820
TURN RIGHT AT HOTEL 3-WAY INTERSECTION

8
00:48.903 --> 00:51.406
PARKING LOT ELECTRICAL PANEL ACROSS FROM JANGMI BUILDING - K

9
03:05.915 --> 03:08.084
THE BLUE ROAD

10
03:11.421 --> 03:13.798
BODY FOUND AHEAD OF OLYMPIC OPENING

11
03:15.466 --> 03:18.386
They've become more brutal and meticulous than before.

12
03:19.345 --> 03:21.014
Have they evolved on their own?

13
03:32.900 --> 03:36.863
Come on! We can't lose against Korea.

14
03:43.578 --> 03:45.830
If they lose to Japan, they should commit seppuku.

15
03:51.044 --> 03:52.295
Why is that?

16
03:57.675 --> 04:00.053
Because those bastards are hell-bent on killing us.

17
04:09.228 --> 04:10.229
You.

18
04:14.484 --> 04:15.568
Hello there.

19
04:22.742 --> 04:24.494
What's with the tough-guy act?

20
04:26.245 --> 04:28.164
You guys must be the yakuza.

21
04:29.374 --> 04:30.375
This little shit.

22
04:31.667 --> 04:33.294
You're Inspector Kim Seok, right?

23
04:34.295 --> 04:36.381
Calm down and hear us out, will you?

24
04:36.464 --> 04:38.674
Identify yourselves properly first.

25
04:41.636 --> 04:42.887
An eyewitness.

26
04:49.894 --> 04:51.479
You still haven't found one, no?

27
05:10.623 --> 05:17.130
TAMPOPO PACHINKO

28
05:36.399 --> 05:37.483
Welcome back.

29
05:54.167 --> 05:55.042
Sit.

30
05:59.130 --> 06:02.216
One of my men overheard this Chinese junkie

31
06:02.717 --> 06:05.344
running his mouth at a bulgogi restaurant in Shibuya.

32
06:06.345 --> 06:08.723
Saying he was right there,

33
06:09.223 --> 06:11.058
that he witnessed the scene.

34
06:14.020 --> 06:17.148
So you thought you'd kidnap him, lock him up, and threaten him?

35
06:17.899 --> 06:19.108
Detective.

36
06:21.903 --> 06:23.571
Take the offer while it stands.

37
06:24.989 --> 06:27.575
You're dying to know, aren't you?

38
06:30.411 --> 06:31.579
Continue.

39
06:32.788 --> 06:35.833
Say it again. From the top.

40
06:38.669 --> 06:40.379
That abandoned building…

41
06:40.880 --> 06:44.842
Shinjuku junkies use it all the time as a meetup spot.

42
06:45.426 --> 06:49.013
He says that abandoned building is a frequent meetup spot

43
06:49.096 --> 06:51.265
for Shinjuku junkies.

44
06:51.766 --> 06:53.643
Did you know the dead girl?

45
06:55.061 --> 06:56.020
Miyashita Aki.

46
06:56.604 --> 06:57.855
You knew her, right?

47
06:58.814 --> 07:00.066
I did.

48
07:00.650 --> 07:04.153
We hung out a few times, got high together.

49
07:05.029 --> 07:07.698
But then she said she found someone selling for less.

50
07:07.782 --> 07:10.034
I didn't see her much after that.

51
07:16.832 --> 07:18.042
That day…

52
08:03.588 --> 08:06.424
Aki's arms and legs were completely twisted.

53
08:07.091 --> 08:08.676
What I then saw…

54
08:10.303 --> 08:13.514
No, it wasn't human.

55
08:16.309 --> 08:19.145
That thing was no human. It was a monster!

56
08:21.647 --> 08:22.732
A tiger!

57
08:24.900 --> 08:26.861
A tiger monster!

58
08:31.407 --> 08:32.325
Get up.

59
08:37.496 --> 08:39.123
The Japanese police

60
08:39.624 --> 08:41.834
keep trying to link us to this case.

61
08:42.335 --> 08:43.794
It's becoming a real pain.

62
08:46.797 --> 08:49.008
We helped you out first this time.

63
08:50.426 --> 08:53.554
Next time, we'll be expecting a big favor in return.

64
09:04.106 --> 09:06.817
Pull a reckless stunt like this one more time,

65
09:07.860 --> 09:09.945
and I'll be the first to arrest you.

66
09:13.032 --> 09:14.200
ITO MAKOTO

67
09:14.283 --> 09:16.994
My boss wanted me to tell you that he is a fellow compatriot

68
09:17.495 --> 09:20.790
you can rely on in times of need.

69
09:20.873 --> 09:24.960
SEO HYUN-TAE

70
09:42.603 --> 09:45.064
Back in Korea in the '80s…

71
09:47.858 --> 09:51.153
a body was found with twisted limbs.

72
09:55.408 --> 09:57.118
And then, there were more.

73
09:59.662 --> 10:00.621
The killer

74
10:01.414 --> 10:02.998
has returned.

75
10:16.887 --> 10:18.806
Interesting.

76
10:28.691 --> 10:31.527
The eyewitness was indeed a junkie.

77
10:41.954 --> 10:46.041
It seems the killer lured Miyashita Aki with the promise of cheaper drugs.

78
10:46.125 --> 10:47.084
And…

79
10:52.339 --> 10:53.382
What is it?

80
10:54.884 --> 10:57.178
Are you going to keep going rogue like this?

81
10:57.678 --> 11:00.848
When you told me about the similar bodies

82
11:00.931 --> 11:03.142
found years ago in Korea,

83
11:03.225 --> 11:05.728
weren't you suggesting we work together?

84
11:06.937 --> 11:07.855
I guess so.

85
11:08.397 --> 11:09.857
In that case,

86
11:09.940 --> 11:12.318
no more secrets from now on.

87
11:12.401 --> 11:13.444
Whatsoever.

88
11:16.071 --> 11:16.989
All right.

89
11:17.656 --> 11:18.741
Understood.

90
11:24.371 --> 11:25.581
You're being serious?

91
11:37.051 --> 11:38.010
Here.

92
11:40.387 --> 11:42.723
The junkie said he saw some tiger.

93
11:44.308 --> 11:46.477
The information was from one of Ito's people?

94
11:47.394 --> 11:49.772
Is he famous?

95
11:49.855 --> 11:51.649
His Korean name is Seo Hyun-tae.

96
11:52.149 --> 11:54.360
He's a big name in Tokyo's pachinko industry.

97
11:54.443 --> 11:58.030
But no one's actually seen him before.

98
11:58.113 --> 12:01.325
He's the type to keep a low profile.

99
12:02.993 --> 12:05.746
So that woman must be his second-in-command or something.

100
12:06.497 --> 12:07.998
It's all clicking now.

101
12:08.499 --> 12:11.126
Word is that Ito dipped his toes into the drug trade

102
12:11.210 --> 12:13.254
alongside his pachinko business.

103
12:14.004 --> 12:15.506
Though there's no proof.

104
12:17.758 --> 12:21.470
I bet they caught the Chinese junkie so fast

105
12:21.554 --> 12:23.305
because he's a Speed K supplier.

106
12:23.389 --> 12:24.682
Speed K…

107
12:25.474 --> 12:29.728
Either way, the information from that woman still lacks specifics.

108
12:30.229 --> 12:34.692
So let's start with you telling me about the Korean case from the '80s.

109
12:36.861 --> 12:39.280
Well, this is quite the morning welcome.

110
12:39.363 --> 12:41.323
Are you out of your mind?!

111
12:42.658 --> 12:44.994
What do you take the Tokyo Police for?!

112
12:45.870 --> 12:48.539
Pack your bags and go back to Korea right now!

113
12:53.627 --> 12:55.838
This is unbelievable.

114
12:56.338 --> 12:57.923
I'll fill you in another time.

115
13:01.468 --> 13:02.428
What?

116
13:04.263 --> 13:05.639
No way.

117
13:05.723 --> 13:09.226
So he played both the Japanese and Korean police?

118
13:09.310 --> 13:12.104
Forging official paperwork so quickly is pretty impressive.

119
13:13.230 --> 13:16.191
You think this is funny? You talk like it's not your problem.

120
13:16.275 --> 13:18.819
I didn't mean it like that, sir.

121
13:23.073 --> 13:24.992
What's going to happen to that Korean?

122
13:25.492 --> 13:29.204
It looks like the higher-ups accepted an apology behind the scenes.

123
13:29.872 --> 13:32.875
So it'll probably blow over with a forced deportation.

124
13:34.043 --> 13:36.754
Leniency like this is practically unheard of.

125
13:36.837 --> 13:38.505
Leniency?

126
13:39.256 --> 13:42.509
The department's only letting it slide to save face.

127
13:42.593 --> 13:43.552
Inose.

128
13:43.636 --> 13:45.304
Talk like that

129
13:45.888 --> 13:46.805
is a no-no.

130
13:47.806 --> 13:50.935
Aren't you the least bit angry?

131
14:22.675 --> 14:25.135
Why does he look so darn smug?

132
14:26.804 --> 14:29.682
I wonder…

133
14:34.478 --> 14:35.479
What is it?

134
14:35.980 --> 14:37.314
What are you up to now?

135
14:38.565 --> 14:40.693
I'm just curious what goes on…

136
14:42.653 --> 14:46.865
inside the head of a guy who's willing to throw away his badge to solve a case.

137
14:53.747 --> 14:55.791
They're two of a kind.

138
14:56.834 --> 15:01.463
And that's exactly why, sir, you're an outcast.

139
15:12.182 --> 15:14.226
Wait. Hey!

140
15:14.309 --> 15:15.310
Hold it!

141
15:17.855 --> 15:18.939
What are you doing?

142
15:22.484 --> 15:23.402
You

143
15:24.111 --> 15:25.779
did that on purpose, didn't you?

144
15:27.906 --> 15:28.949
What do you mean?

145
15:31.118 --> 15:32.911
You brought up that old case

146
15:32.995 --> 15:35.247
to get me to act, didn't you?

147
15:38.792 --> 15:40.669
I just wanted to catch the culprit.

148
15:41.170 --> 15:42.254
That's all.

149
15:44.006 --> 15:45.758
Before the list of victims grows.

150
15:48.510 --> 15:51.597
I'm going to catch them, too, you know. The culprit.

151
15:53.557 --> 15:54.808
No matter what.

152
16:09.448 --> 16:10.991
I apologize for the trouble.

153
16:29.051 --> 16:32.012
Your luggage at the hotel will be sent to you later.

154
16:32.096 --> 16:35.641
You may depart right away.

155
16:41.230 --> 16:43.774
DETECTIVE, I FOUND THE SOURCE OF THE PHRASE AT THE SCENE

156
16:43.857 --> 16:45.818
FROM: PROF. JANG (DEPT. OF CRIMINAL HISTORY)

157
18:45.938 --> 18:52.486
"ONE FEAR BREEDS INFINITE FEAR AND ALL METHODS SHALL BE CONCEALED."

158
18:52.569 --> 18:54.821
THE TALE OF EMIRI, HIDDEN HERO OF THE IMJIN WAR 3

159
18:54.905 --> 18:56.281
POST PUBLISHED

160
18:56.365 --> 19:03.330
SEOUL METROPOLITAN POLICE AGENCY

161
19:06.166 --> 19:08.669
MOBILE INVESTIGATION UNIT

162
19:09.294 --> 19:11.672
Scared? I'll put my back into it this time.

163
19:11.755 --> 19:14.174
Bam! What are you doing? Get up.

164
19:16.843 --> 19:17.928
Jjajangmyeon again?

165
19:18.011 --> 19:18.845
Let's eat.

166
19:19.346 --> 19:21.556
-Thank you for the meal! -Enjoy your meal.

167
19:21.640 --> 19:22.933
Bro, come eat first!

168
19:23.016 --> 19:25.811
-Eat. -All right, you lumps. Let's eat.

169
19:25.894 --> 19:27.521
Say thank you before you pig out.

170
19:27.604 --> 19:29.523
-Thank you. -Thank you for the food!

171
19:32.609 --> 19:33.860
Is it good?

172
19:33.944 --> 19:36.780
Go on. Eat up.

173
19:36.863 --> 19:37.698
Hey!

174
19:56.633 --> 19:57.467
Hey!

175
20:10.731 --> 20:13.900
You reckless bastard. You don't give a damn about rules, do you?

176
20:14.943 --> 20:17.237
I knew you'd cause trouble one day.

177
20:17.321 --> 20:20.198
But you just had to go and embarrass our fucking country

178
20:20.282 --> 20:21.867
in Japan of all places…

179
20:23.910 --> 20:26.955
What are you, on the national team? Is this about the World Cup?

180
20:27.873 --> 20:29.833
You think your track record makes you untouchable?

181
20:29.916 --> 20:31.543
You're in for disciplinary action.

182
20:32.044 --> 20:33.211
What if…

183
20:35.047 --> 20:37.215
I let you take some of my credit?

184
20:38.425 --> 20:39.259
What?

185
20:40.260 --> 20:41.470
That doesn't interest you?

186
20:43.263 --> 20:45.349
You scratch my back, I scratch yours, sir.

187
20:46.391 --> 20:48.101
Look here, Inspector Kim.

188
20:50.395 --> 20:53.398
What the hell do you take me for, you son of a bitch?

189
20:53.482 --> 20:55.567
"You scratch my back, I scratch yours"?

190
20:55.650 --> 20:57.027
I dare you to say that again.

191
20:57.527 --> 20:59.696
Say that again, you bastard!

192
21:00.280 --> 21:01.406
Chief Gu.

193
21:02.032 --> 21:04.409
I'm sorry to interrupt, sir,

194
21:05.035 --> 21:07.537
but someone's here to see Inspector Kim Seok.

195
21:07.621 --> 21:08.663
Who?

196
21:18.965 --> 21:19.800
Can we help you?

197
21:24.096 --> 21:25.138
Yakuza?

198
21:28.809 --> 21:29.935
Cute.

199
21:31.561 --> 21:32.854
What the hell is this?

200
21:36.608 --> 21:37.567
The hell are you?

201
21:38.276 --> 21:39.361
What?

202
21:51.540 --> 21:52.791
Long time no see.

203
22:01.425 --> 22:02.926
Your outfit is…

204
22:04.428 --> 22:05.303
"Outfit"?

205
22:07.013 --> 22:08.014
Well, your out--

206
22:08.098 --> 22:09.474
Wait a minute.

207
22:14.062 --> 22:16.773
ACHIEVE PERFECTION! TRAIN YOUR KOREAN

208
22:17.274 --> 22:18.108
Oh, outfit?

209
22:24.197 --> 22:25.449
You here for the World Cup?

210
22:28.076 --> 22:30.871
Unlike you, I'm here on an official assignment.

211
22:37.043 --> 22:39.880
It's all been sorted with your higher-ups as well.

212
22:43.508 --> 22:46.261
They sure processed the official paperwork fast.

213
22:46.761 --> 22:48.221
It's obvious, isn't it?

214
22:49.764 --> 22:52.684
Someone wants this case solved,

215
22:53.185 --> 22:54.978
and it's either one of our bigwigs

216
22:55.479 --> 22:56.938
or that fella.

217
22:58.231 --> 23:00.108
The guy behind the pachinko business?

218
23:00.859 --> 23:01.943
Seo Hyun-tae?

219
23:06.740 --> 23:11.077
Whatever the case, I don't care as long as I can catch the killer.

220
23:14.873 --> 23:16.416
Anyway, let catch him.

221
23:20.337 --> 23:21.463
Let's catch him.

222
23:22.005 --> 23:23.757
Anyway, let's catch him.

223
23:25.300 --> 23:26.134
Let's catch him.

224
23:26.218 --> 23:28.929
Anyway, follow me. There's someone we need to meet.

225
23:37.312 --> 23:38.772
Thank you for seeing us, Professor.

226
23:38.855 --> 23:40.190
PROFESSOR JANG GYEONG-SEOB

227
23:40.273 --> 23:41.399
I'm more than happy to.

228
23:41.483 --> 23:42.651
Here.

229
23:44.528 --> 23:45.820
Thank you for the drink.

230
23:45.904 --> 23:47.572
Sure. Cheers.

231
23:48.740 --> 23:49.616
Go ahead.

232
23:53.036 --> 23:58.416
I've already briefly told other folks about the origin of the phrase.

233
23:58.500 --> 24:02.295
According to historical records, during the Imjin War,

234
24:02.379 --> 24:05.840
a general named Emiri naturalized to help Joseon.

235
24:07.467 --> 24:09.261
If you look at this painting…

236
24:09.344 --> 24:11.555
Emiri claimed that for the Joseon army to win,

237
24:11.638 --> 24:14.683
it was important to instill fear inside the Japanese troops.

238
24:14.766 --> 24:18.562
And that is likely why he put the enemies' corpses on display.

239
24:20.021 --> 24:21.022
Display…

240
24:27.279 --> 24:28.154
This.

241
24:29.281 --> 24:33.410
"One fear breeds infinite fear and all methods shall be concealed."

242
24:33.994 --> 24:36.621
Yes, the phrase found at the crime scenes.

243
24:36.705 --> 24:41.459
That very phrase appears in Emiri's treatise on military strategy.

244
24:43.044 --> 24:46.131
At the time, Emiri fought as a general in the Joseon army

245
24:46.214 --> 24:48.967
and was infamous for his brutal methods.

246
24:53.471 --> 24:56.641
He would drug the Japanese soldiers with poppies…

247
24:58.810 --> 25:02.439
tie them to a torture rack, and brutally twist their limbs.

248
25:05.609 --> 25:08.778
And it is said that he displayed the grotesquely misshapen bodies

249
25:08.862 --> 25:12.824
alongside the phrase, written in blood.

250
25:13.992 --> 25:17.787
All to spread fear among the enemy ranks.

251
25:20.332 --> 25:24.419
To think that a Joseon dynasty tale is being reenacted in the 21st century…

252
25:24.502 --> 25:25.962
It's quite astonishing.

253
25:28.423 --> 25:30.800
This just occurred to me.

254
25:32.010 --> 25:36.306
If Emiri really did exist, might there be descendants of his?

255
25:37.557 --> 25:41.936
After the war, most Japanese soldiers who had surrendered stayed in Joseon.

256
25:42.020 --> 25:45.440
But it seems their lives afterward were far from easy.

257
25:45.940 --> 25:48.568
Some accounts say they had a rough time adjusting.

258
25:49.361 --> 25:52.489
In Emiri's case, there's even a theory that he was betrayed and killed

259
25:52.572 --> 25:54.783
by a subordinate who naturalized with him.

260
25:55.283 --> 25:56.451
Betrayed?

261
25:56.534 --> 25:57.786
Killed?

262
25:58.912 --> 26:02.874
The theory goes that he was killed by a Japanese spy,

263
26:02.957 --> 26:05.710
planted to prepare for the next war.

264
26:06.711 --> 26:08.797
His subordinate was a Japanese spy.

265
26:09.964 --> 26:13.385
What's interesting is that while hardly any records of Emiri exist in Korea,

266
26:14.386 --> 26:17.764
there were some in Japan who remembered him,

267
26:17.847 --> 26:19.849
even worshiping him as a god.

268
26:21.101 --> 26:23.395
Japan has no shortage of gods, after all.

269
26:23.478 --> 26:26.606
It's said they even worship General Yi Sun-sin as a god of war.

270
26:29.651 --> 26:32.779
There are people who worship Emiri as a god.

271
26:36.408 --> 26:38.159
A Korea-Japan joint investigation?

272
26:38.660 --> 26:39.786
Damn it.

273
26:43.540 --> 26:44.541
Chief!

274
26:45.709 --> 26:46.584
Chief.

275
26:47.127 --> 26:50.088
Someone posted this on an online forum the week Park In-gyu died.

276
26:50.171 --> 26:51.464
I'm not in the mood to talk.

277
26:51.548 --> 26:54.050
There's something fishy about this. I think you should--

278
26:54.134 --> 26:54.968
The hell is it?!

279
26:55.927 --> 26:59.305
It's about the origin of that phrase at the scene, from the Imjin War…

280
26:59.389 --> 27:03.560
The source that Professor Jang, Detective Kim's informant, mentioned.

281
27:03.643 --> 27:04.728
You know…

282
27:05.478 --> 27:06.521
The…

283
27:06.604 --> 27:08.565
What? What is it?

284
27:08.648 --> 27:10.900
Some anonymous guy posts a history lesson online,

285
27:10.984 --> 27:14.154
not even on the same day but week, and you're saying he's the culprit?

286
27:14.237 --> 27:16.614
Is that it? Sure! Why the hell not?

287
27:18.283 --> 27:19.409
Dumbass.

288
27:19.492 --> 27:20.493
I'm sorry, sir.

289
27:21.077 --> 27:23.288
-Then I'll discuss this Kim-- -Why, you little…

290
27:23.371 --> 27:24.456
Hey.

291
27:27.667 --> 27:29.294
Track the IP address, I guess.

292
27:32.380 --> 27:34.507
-And who do you report back to? -To you, Chief.

293
27:35.967 --> 27:36.926
Loyalty.

294
27:37.510 --> 27:39.846
-Good day, sir. -Damn Inspector Kim.

295
27:39.929 --> 27:41.014
You motherfucker.

296
27:46.227 --> 27:47.395
CYBER CRIMES UNIT

297
27:47.479 --> 27:49.773
Track the IP address…

298
27:51.608 --> 27:52.442
MESSAGE SENT

299
27:53.026 --> 27:55.695
If you need anything, please don't hesitate to contact me.

300
27:55.779 --> 27:57.363
-Yes, I will. -Great.

301
27:57.447 --> 27:58.448
Thank you.

302
28:03.161 --> 28:04.871
What a sad history.

303
28:13.463 --> 28:14.964
What's so sad about it?

304
28:15.048 --> 28:16.925
Emiri's life is tragic.

305
28:17.425 --> 28:20.094
He even naturalized, only to be betrayed by one of his men.

306
28:20.595 --> 28:23.890
There'd be nothing to be sad about if your people hadn't started the war.

307
28:25.517 --> 28:27.310
Well, that stings.

308
28:29.521 --> 28:30.772
I came to Korea

309
28:31.523 --> 28:33.316
to help.

310
28:35.068 --> 28:36.027
To help?

311
28:36.528 --> 28:37.403
Yes.

312
28:38.196 --> 28:39.364
Who's helping who?

313
28:42.367 --> 28:43.993
We're catching them together.

314
28:44.577 --> 28:46.704
Let's get that straight, okay?

315
28:56.714 --> 28:58.842
EX-WIFE GOT CHILD SUPPORT, TUITION'S DUE NEXT WEEK

316
28:58.925 --> 28:59.884
Come on.

317
29:02.971 --> 29:05.139
I guess I've got a pretty sad story myself.

318
29:14.941 --> 29:15.859
Hello, Chief.

319
29:15.942 --> 29:17.819
You met Professor Jang, didn't you?

320
29:17.902 --> 29:21.114
Emiri, right? The Imjin War!

321
29:22.740 --> 29:25.034
Get a move on! What are you doing, you slowpokes?

322
29:25.118 --> 29:26.369
Yes, sir!

323
29:26.953 --> 29:28.162
This bastard basically wrote

324
29:28.246 --> 29:30.832
the whole Veritable Records of the Joseon Dynasty online.

325
29:31.332 --> 29:32.292
What do you mean?

326
29:32.375 --> 29:33.751
You dimwit.

327
29:33.835 --> 29:38.006
This needy bastard just can't help crying for attention.

328
29:38.089 --> 29:40.174
They're non-stop posting about Emiri.

329
29:40.258 --> 29:41.801
And here's the kicker.

330
29:41.885 --> 29:46.514
"One fear breeds infinite fear and all methods shall be concealed."

331
29:46.598 --> 29:48.600
It's in the post. We have our guy!

332
29:48.683 --> 29:52.020
You said you'd scratch my back, remember? Thanks for the credit.

333
29:52.103 --> 29:55.440
Hold up. Are you mad? Then make sure to bring your gun.

334
29:56.190 --> 29:58.318
Because I'm gonna shoot your ass.

335
30:00.111 --> 30:01.237
To Yangpyeong! Now!

336
30:31.976 --> 30:33.895
Let's go! Follow me!

337
30:33.978 --> 30:35.229
Yes, sir!

338
30:35.730 --> 30:38.316
-Team 1, get the warehouse door! -Yes, sir!

339
30:38.399 --> 30:40.026
-Team 2, through the front! -Sir!

340
30:40.109 --> 30:42.278
Let's move inside. Keep up!

341
30:42.904 --> 30:43.738
Team 3, over here!

342
30:43.821 --> 30:44.864
Yes, sir!

343
30:45.573 --> 30:47.992
What the hell is this? Did they lock someone up in here?

344
30:48.076 --> 30:49.744
Hey! Hurry and get inside!

345
30:49.827 --> 30:52.413
Keep it down. Watch your footsteps, you oaf!

346
30:53.206 --> 30:54.207
-Ha In-beom. -This way.

347
30:54.290 --> 30:55.208
Inspector Kim…

348
30:56.042 --> 30:57.543
That son of a bitch.

349
31:53.933 --> 31:55.393
Team 1, suspect not found.

350
31:56.310 --> 31:57.854
Team 2, suspect not found.

351
31:59.230 --> 32:01.065
Team 3, suspect not found.

352
32:03.651 --> 32:06.362
Are we sure this is the place, Chief? There's nothing here.

353
32:06.446 --> 32:08.573
-I think it's a bust, Chief. -Follow me out.

354
32:08.656 --> 32:10.366
I'm about to lose it.

355
32:13.411 --> 32:14.704
Wait.

356
32:15.246 --> 32:16.831
-What? -Inose.

357
32:18.875 --> 32:21.419
IP tracking usually has a pretty wide margin of error.

358
32:22.754 --> 32:23.880
The antenna over there.

359
32:24.464 --> 32:26.799
The internet.

360
32:29.260 --> 32:30.303
Let's go.

361
32:30.386 --> 32:31.220
Yeah.

362
32:32.889 --> 32:34.182
Watch your step.

363
32:44.776 --> 32:46.652
What incredible momentum.

364
32:46.736 --> 32:50.364
They cut through the opposition with a series of rapid midfield passes.

365
32:50.448 --> 32:51.824
To the left side, there's…

366
33:15.056 --> 33:16.099
That's soccer for you.

367
33:16.182 --> 33:18.976
The most dangerous moment often comes after a missed chance.

368
33:19.060 --> 33:24.107
And the opposition wins it back, immediately sending a long ball forward!

369
33:24.190 --> 33:27.693
The defense had pushed way up to focus on the attack!

370
33:27.777 --> 33:29.570
Their backline's completely exposed!

371
33:29.654 --> 33:32.198
They're in trouble. The defenders need to sprint back.

372
33:32.281 --> 33:36.244
Instead of rushing in to defend, they should use delay tactics to buy time…

373
33:36.327 --> 33:37.870
Looks like they were just here.

374
33:37.954 --> 33:40.456
The opposing striker cuts into the right side of the box.

375
33:40.540 --> 33:43.835
The defender fights desperately for the ball, but the opposition--

376
34:06.107 --> 34:07.191
One.

377
34:08.151 --> 34:09.235
Two.

378
34:10.987 --> 34:11.904
Three.

379
34:15.700 --> 34:16.993
Hands up!

380
34:18.703 --> 34:20.121
-Don't move. -The heck?

381
34:21.664 --> 34:22.707
Calm down.

382
34:22.790 --> 34:24.250
They're just kids!

383
34:27.044 --> 34:27.920
Outside!

384
34:43.811 --> 34:46.022
I'll pay you back. I swear!

385
34:48.733 --> 34:49.817
Who are you?

386
34:52.153 --> 34:53.070
What?

387
34:53.154 --> 34:54.405
Didn't Mr. Park send you?

388
34:55.364 --> 34:57.033
What did you just say?

389
34:57.533 --> 34:59.076
Well, who are you, then?

390
35:01.287 --> 35:02.371
Detective Kim.

391
35:05.249 --> 35:06.500
What does this say?

392
35:08.544 --> 35:09.754
It was inside.

393
35:09.837 --> 35:11.964
MANAGE ONLINE OPINION COMMENT WRITING SERVICES

394
35:12.048 --> 35:13.257
Paid commenters?

395
36:58.362 --> 37:00.281
UNUSUAL NIGHTTIME DISTURBANCE IN YANGPYEONG

396
37:00.364 --> 37:03.701
POLICE LARGE-SCALE OPERATION FAILS DESPITE CUTTING-EDGE IP TRACKING TECH

397
37:03.784 --> 37:06.746
GENERAL EMIRI

398
41:31.176 --> 41:34.680
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
